# OPTIONAL — you do not need this file to build the installer.
#
# By default the ISO contains no password. The server machine generates its
# own login the first time it boots, shows it on its screen and in Suite
# Manager, and deletes it once you confirm you have saved it.
# Your Suite Manager owner account is NOT configured here; it is created
# in the browser after the first boot.
#
# To pin any value, copy this file to selfhost-installer.env in the same
# folder and uncomment the lines you want:

# Pinning this bakes the password into the ISO. Useful for a lab machine you
# reset often; never publish or share an ISO built this way, because the image
# is the password. The Hyper-V smoke lab does not need this — it already builds
# with a fixed known login (mos / admin1234) so agents can SSH in unprompted.
# LINUX_PASSWORD=your-machine-login-password
# STACK_DOMAIN=mos.home
# TIMEZONE=Europe/Copenhagen
# HOSTNAME=mos
# USERNAME=mos
# REALNAME=My Own Suite
